1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,339
The siren had sounded six minutes earlier.

2
00:00:04,339 --> 00:00:09,058
David Levy, seventy-two, did not go down to the shelter.

3
00:00:09,058 --> 00:00:12,260
He had lived through 1967, 1973, 2006.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:14,704
He had heard too many sirens.

5
00:00:14,704 --> 00:00:16,642
He stood at his window.

6
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:21,782
In the early morning, Ramat Gan glowed the color of a sunset.

7
00:00:21,782 --> 00:00:23,383
The glass trembled.

8
00:00:23,383 --> 00:00:27,006
The next moment, he was lying on the floor.

9
00:00:27,006 --> 00:00:29,955
The sound had gone out of his ears.

10
00:00:29,955 --> 00:00:35,011
The ceiling was cracked, and dust drifted down. This is war.

11
00:00:35,011 --> 00:00:37,876
Not because I didn't take shelter.

12
00:00:37,876 --> 00:00:40,910
Because the war came looking for me.

13
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:43,185
Civilians never choose war.

14
00:00:43,185 --> 00:00:45,966
But war always chooses civilians.

